// Generated game supplements; rebuild with scripts/sync-game-profiles.mjs.
export const GAME_PROFILE_PROMPTS = {
  "common": "[GAME PROFILE CONTRACT — MECHANICS, NOT SETTING]\nThe selected profile supplies mechanics at the chosen quality's existing preparation horizon and board budget. It does not create a setting, genre, faction, required encounter or character ability. Record edition, source/errata, options and exceptions in [MISC #ruleset]. Preserve existing canon and sheet; switching the selector alone is not character conversion or permission to overwrite an incompatible campaign. Resolve a material source/sheet conflict before the affected action, without resetting the world.\n\nUse real tool receipts for required direct randomness. Fix purpose, relevant pool/target/opposition and applicable costs before the result. Preserve individual dice when the system needs them; a summed total cannot stand in for a pool, a critical pair or separate regular/special dice. If the tool cannot expose the needed dice, roll separate supported formulas or use a supplied verifiable manual result; do not invent faces. Rules-authorized pushes, rerolls, resource spending and recovery remain available with their actual eligibility and timing. Record the cost and every original/replacement receipt and apply the rule's keep/replacement semantics. This never authorizes rerolling during technical retries, review or repair. An unresolved optional player choice stays a choice, not silently spent resources or extra voluntary actions. For private play, resolve required legal rolls during simulation; if a reviewer discovers that an indispensable roll was never made, preserve the draft and report the missing resolution instead of manufacturing it.\n\nApply the core's explicit deterministic, no-dice convention to wholly off-screen uncertainty. Record it as a campaign convention distinct from official random rules. Aggregate uneventful progress; do not invent critical faces, table results or statistical success as if a random check happened. Direct encounters retain the selected system's actual resolution. All participants share one objective interval; rounds/turns/actions use this system's duration, not another system's example.\n\nRetain a relevant person's actual loyalties and their beneficiaries, incentives, debts, refusal boundaries, knowledge and consequential relationships before they govern influence. Preserve established scales, bribery terms, vices and family ties; do not manufacture vulnerabilities or a price for every NPC. Influence follows actual system rules and circumstances. It cannot reveal unknown information or backfill a lever after success. Established supernatural effects retain their source-defined scope; a generic red line supplies no unstated immunity. The player authors voluntary feelings, interpretations, commitments and choices. A confirmed rules-imposed involuntary condition may be recorded and applied only within its verified source, trigger, resistance/result, scope and duration; it grants no extra knowledge, unrelated feelings or further voluntary actions. Preserve disclosure boundaries and explicit campaign agreements.\n\nWorld time and real-play/session cadence are different quantities. Keep a separately identified agreed session/play-time marker when the selected rules use one. A message, review, reload, technical retry, API latency or fictional travel is not by itself a new session or play-time recharge. If a required cadence is unknown in asynchronous play, leave the affected refresh/choice unresolved until agreed; never silently derive it from the world clock. There is still only one fictional world interval.\n\nUse required source rules and supplied sheet values; resolve missing indispensable parameters rather than fabricate a source citation or a rule table. HUD and item cards show only relevant player-known mechanics and discovered properties. The selected profile supplies its own advancement procedure; the common contract grants no calculator or schema to another system.\n",
  "advancement": "[CAMPAIGN-OWNED ADVANCEMENT]\nWhen advancement applies, use [MISC #character_progression] as a persistent campaign-owned record: starting earned state, uniquely identified dated awards/development, point spending or applied changes with their sources/costs, remaining balance and unresolved player choices. Update the sheet and record together, retain previous entries through compression, and do not award or spend twice on a retry. Apply only legitimate prospective changes; advancement is not an automatic rest or cure. If the campaign has no formal progression, do not invent a numeric advancement subsystem.\n\nThe extension does NOT calculate this profile's progression, success rules, feature legality or resource costs. Do not import the D&D version-1 XP/classes/proficiency schema as a requirement of this profile. Preserve an already established campaign record without conversion; a separately agreed mechanism may remain in use. Resolve missing indispensable parameters from the adopted rules and supplied sheet, not fabricated tables or source citations.\n",
  "coc7e": "[GAME SYSTEM PROFILE — CALL OF CTHULHU 7TH EDITION]\nThis profile supplies mechanics, not a setting, era, plot, tone or larger preparation horizon. Record the campaign's edition, printing, Keeper Rulebook / Investigator Handbook or explicitly adopted introductory source, options and exceptions in `[MISC #ruleset]`; preserve an existing selection, including Quick-Start or Starter Set. If none is established, use standard 7th Edition core scope (Keeper Rulebook, with Investigator Handbook material where applicable), not an automatic Quick-Start restriction; do not silently add Pulp Cthulhu talents or survivability rules. Introductory references can confirm shared basics but do not replace missing full-core procedures. If an essential spell, table, injury rule or option is unspecified, identify and resolve the missing parameter from the adopted source before resolving it; do not invent a rule and call it official.\n\n**Investigator.** Keep the existing player's `[ENTITIES #id]`: STR, CON, SIZ, DEX, APP, INT, POW and EDU; age and occupation; skill percentages and relevant specializations; current/maximum HP and MP; current Luck; current/maximum SAN; Cthulhu Mythos; damage bonus, Build, movement and Dodge; actual weapons, ammunition, malfunctions, armor, possessions and wealth; injuries and conditions. Preserve earned and spent values. Retain supplied backstory, beliefs and significant people without authoring the player's personality or past. Maximum SAN is 99 minus Cthulhu Mythos; derive other values under the selected source, retaining documented exceptions.\n\n**Checks and receipts.** Roll only for consequential uncertainty. Establish goal, skill/characteristic, required success level, modifiers and stakes before the tool call. Use real dice-tool receipts: normally `1d100`, with 100 representing percentile 00. Regular success is at or below the full value, Hard at or below its rounded-down half, Extreme at or below its rounded-down fifth. Preserve natural critical/fumble results under the selected source: 01 is critical and 100 fumbles; apply its wider 96–100 fumble range where applicable. Establish that applicability from the adopted rule, not merely an assumption that demanding Hard/Extreme success changes the fumble range. Do not substitute another BRP game's critical table. Opposed checks compare success levels, then actual skill values for equal levels, with the governing tie procedure; combat has its own exceptions.\n\nBonus/penalty dice change the percentile tens digit, not two complete d100 rolls. Cancel opposing bonus and penalty dice, then use the source's limits. Roll one shared units digit plus the ordinary and additional tens digits independently; a tool `1d10` result of 10 maps to digit 0. Assemble each candidate with that same units digit; 00 means 100. Take the lowest candidate for bonus dice or highest for penalty dice. Retain the component receipts and selected result. Never invent a bonus digit or use D&D advantage notation as a substitute.\n\nA justified push is a second attempt with changed effort/risk and actual time, not a free reroll. Obtain the player's decision, establish likely failure consequences, then roll once where pushing is legal. No pushing combat, Luck, SAN, damage or SAN-loss rolls. If optional Luck spending is enabled, a player may lower an eligible result point for point from current Luck; retain original roll, cost and adjusted result. Do not spend it for the player without delegation. It cannot change pushed or fumbled rolls, malfunctions, Luck/SAN checks, damage or SAN-loss amounts. Rereading receipts, revising the board or checking arithmetic never permits a fresh roll or repeated cost.\n\n**Luck and objective preparation.** A Luck roll uses current Luck; a group roll uses the lowest Luck among the relevant investigators. Standard rules can use Luck to establish uncertain external circumstances. This profile uses a declared **closed-world Luck house convention**, not unchanged CoC RAW: record the policy in `[MISC #ruleset]` and disclose it briefly when first establishing campaign rules. Selecting this profile alone does not authorize fact creation by Luck. It cannot replace a prepared fact, populate a closed empty inventory or create the item sought by a search; use an applicable skill to discover actual prepared facts, but do not claim a skill can make an external circumstance exist. For genuinely undefined external circumstances, retain the closed-world default unless the campaign explicitly agrees on a scoped Luck exception before dependent resolution; record that agreement, its boundary and the resulting fact. A Luck exception is not blanket permission to rewrite prepared contents or history. Preserve an already agreed policy, and never describe this restriction as a universal CoC rule.\n\n**Action and injury.** Follow DEX order and legal actions/responses, with drawn-firearm, surprise, outnumbering, Build, maneuver and range rules when applicable. A round lasts enough time for the participants' significant actions; it is not automatically D&D's six seconds. Record the actual shared duration once. In melee a successful attack ties favor the attacker against fighting back, but the defender against Dodge; both failures do not inflict an ordinary hit. Fighting back does not gain initiating-attack extreme damage. Resolve firearm shots, ammunition, cover, armor and damage under their source. Track major wounds, unconsciousness, dying, stabilization, healing time and instant-death thresholds; neither a scene transition nor advancement restores pools.\n\n**Sanity and magic.** Establish a horror's SAN-loss pair before rolling current SAN, then apply the success/failure branch and actual loss dice. Track cumulative losses and their defined day/baseline for indefinite insanity; do not repeatedly lower the baseline after each loss. A loss of at least five from one SAN check invokes the applicable INT/temporary-insanity procedure. Record bout, duration, treatment and recovery under the source, distinguishing any mechanically imposed perception from world truth. These explicit effects can temporarily constrain player behavior within their rule scope, not grant unlimited control of the character. Do not import nonexistent tables or declare every frightening event a permanent diagnosis. Magic requires actually acquired knowledge and its stated learning/casting time, MP/SAN/other costs and consequences; no automatic spell access from POW or genre.\n\n**Development and social state.** Use a campaign-owned `[MISC #character_progression]` development record with `system: \"coc7e\"`, not the D&D XP schema or levels. Mark eligible successful skills once; at an authorized development phase use the selected source's improvement rolls and gains, excluding skills such as Credit Rating and Cthulhu Mythos from ordinary checks. Keep dated unique award/change IDs, before/after values, roll receipts and unresolved player choices; training and restoration consume their real durations only when the rules require them. Do not reroll development on a revision. Relevant loyalties, debts, family ties, bribe terms and knowledge remain prepared facts independent of Social focus. An influence success cannot supply unknown evidence or invent a matching vulnerability; any actual supernatural effect follows its specified authority.\n\nWholly off-screen processes obey the recorded deterministic campaign convention, explicitly distinct from standard CoC dice adjudication. It never replaces rolls in a direct encounter. Process elapsed time once; keep this profile's conditions, appointments and resource changes consistent with the single clock and the selected quality budget.\n",
  "pf2e": "[GAME SYSTEM PROFILE — PATHFINDER SECOND EDITION REMASTER]\nUse PF2e Remaster (Player Core / GM Core and the campaign's allowed sources). Record approved legacy material, errata and variants explicitly; do not mix PF1e, D&D 5e or legacy versions of a replaced option silently. This profile supplies mechanics, not Golarion lore, a required heroic role or a larger simulation horizon. Follow the selected fidelity's N−1 preparation, closed contents, knowledge separation and single clock.\n\n**Sheet and sources.** Keep each relevant actor's ancestry/heritage, background, class and level, attribute modifiers, proficiency ranks, AC, Fortitude/Reflex/Will, Perception, skills, speeds/senses, languages, attacks/damage and traits, class/spell DCs, current/max/temporary HP, conditions, resistances/weaknesses/immunities, spell repertoire or preparation, slots by rank, Focus Points, Hero Points and equipment. Retain feat names, acquisition levels and governing sources rather than whole rule texts. Record shield Hardness/HP/Broken Threshold, invested items, ammunition, consumables and Bulk when relevant. Never replace an established character with a generated pregen or decide the player's build without delegation.\n\n**Checks.** Before rolling, fix the action, requirements, applicable modifier, target DC and consequence permitted by its actual entry. Use the available dice tool for uncertain direct interaction: usually `1d20` plus the actual modifier. A trained proficiency is level + 2, expert level + 4, master level + 6, legendary level + 8; untrained is normally 0, with recorded exceptions. Include attribute and applicable item/status/circumstance modifiers, respect stacking rules, and do not add level twice. Compare against DC: meeting it succeeds; DC + 10 critically succeeds; DC − 10 or lower critically fails; the intervening below-DC results fail. Natural 20 improves the numerical degree one step, natural 1 worsens it one step; neither guarantees the extreme outcome. Apply further degree adjustments in the governing order. Use the action's listed degree effects; a critical result invents neither extra loot nor a new story power.\n\n**Encounters and clock.** A round is six seconds shared by all actors. Track initiative and remaining three actions / one reaction per turn, adjusted by slowed, stunned, quickened and specific abilities; free actions obey their specified timing and triggers, if any. Movement, Interact, spell activities and skill actions consume their actual costs; do not split an activity or Stride around unrelated actions unless permitted. Reactive Strike is an ability, not a universal opportunity attack. Checks with the attack trait count toward multiple attack penalty: normally −5 on the second attack and −10 on subsequent attacks; an agile attack uses −4/−8. Apply the appropriate penalty to that attack and its timing; Ready has its own off-turn exception. Keep independent NPC activity within the same elapsed interval. Tool calls and review stages do not each advance a round.\n\n**Effects and secrecy.** Apply damage traits, critical damage rules, saves, weaknesses, resistances and immunities in their actual order. Track persistent damage, frightened, dying/wounded, unconsciousness, affliction stages, temporary immunity and effect expiry at their proper boundaries. Respect mental, linguistic, auditory, visual, fortune/misfortune and incapacitation traits: powerful targets can improve their outcome against an incapacitation effect according to spell rank or the originating effect's level. Do not grant an invented immunity merely because an NPC is important. Secret checks still need genuine tool results; keep unrevealed DCs, identities and implications out of prose and player-visible logs. If the configured tool exposes a secret receipt, do not pretend it was hidden; use an available private mechanism or flag that limitation.\n\n**Hero Points.** Under the ordinary Remaster Player Core procedure, begin each agreed game session with 1 Hero Point, award further points for qualifying deeds, cap the balance at 3, and expire unspent points at session end. Preserve explicitly adopted variants and retain session identity and awards/spending in the resource record; a message, model stage, regeneration, reload or API delay is not a session boundary. Spending is the player's choice unless delegated, costs no action and remains available when otherwise unable to act; a point can also be spent for the player's familiar or animal companion. Spend 1 to reroll a check and use the second result even if worse; this is a fortune effect, not unlimited repeated rerolls of the same check. To avoid death when dying would increase, the player may instead spend **all** remaining Hero Points (minimum 1), lose dying and stabilize at 0 HP; this recovery does not add or increase wounded, and does not reduce an existing wounded value. Preserve this choice at its real trigger before finalizing a dependent death; it grants no immunity to an unrelated instant-death effect. Use the selected Remaster wording rather than silently adding a legacy-only trigger. Neither expenditure creates loot or extra character history. Retain the original/replacement receipts and costs exactly once.\n\n**Exploration, recovery and advancement.** Record exploration activities and travel rates; resolve hazards, searches, Treat Wounds, Refocus, repair and downtime with their actual durations, requirements and cooldowns. Rest is not a D&D full reset: use PF2e recovery and daily preparation rules, preserving injuries and spent pools until legitimately recovered. Keep one dated `[MISC #character_progression]` record with `system: \"pf2e\"`, baseline, unique XP awards for completed challenges, applied level, remaining XP, threshold and pending choices. Use a campaign-owned PF2e schema, not D&D's version-1 ledger schema or a second parallel progression block. Normally 1,000 XP earns each level and is deducted, retaining surplus; record another campaign progression rate or milestone method explicitly. Reconcile class features, attribute boosts, skill increases, feats, spells, proficiency and HP with the class's table. Let the player make build choices before applying dependent changes. Advancement does not itself pass fictional time or heal injuries. This is model-maintained state; the extension's D&D XP/level validator does not validate PF2e arithmetic or eligibility.\n\n**Social adjudication.** Use the actual Diplomacy, Deception, Intimidation and relevant subsystems: Make an Impression, Request, Coerce and Demoralize are distinct actions with different prerequisites, durations and outcomes. Establish relevant knowledge, loyalties, incentives, debts, family ties and refusal boundaries before a consequential check where they govern it; do not manufacture a vulnerability or numerical relationship meter for every NPC. Attitude conditions are not omniscience, permanent devotion or control over player choices. Apply actual magical influence within its traits, saves, scope and duration; ordinary conviction is not an unstated immunity. Preserve causal relationship changes when a temporary effect ends.\n\n**Simulation convention and receipts.** Wholly off-screen resolution follows the campaign's recorded deterministic convention. If absent, establish this explicit house convention: fixed die contribution 10 for ordinary d20 checks, rules-based DCs, ordinary average damage, stable initiative by Perception then actor ID; do not fabricate natural 20/1 adjustments or random critical injuries. It is not official PF2e and never substitutes for direct-encounter rolls. Preserve genuine roll receipts and paid costs across retries/reviews; a legal Hero Point or other reroll is a new authorized roll with its resource spent. Missing feat, spell, monster or variant parameters must be resolved from the applicable source or identified as unresolved before deciding the result, never guessed to obtain a desired outcome.\n",
  "gurps4e": "[GAME SYSTEM PROFILE — GURPS FOURTH EDITION]\nThis profile supplies mechanics, not an era, technology level, genre, setting or larger preparation horizon. Record the actual Fourth Edition source and revision, Basic Set versus explicitly adopted GURPS Lite scope, technology level, allowed supplements and optional rules in `[MISC #ruleset]`. Preserve the campaign's source, including an existing Lite selection; otherwise use Fourth Edition Basic Set (Characters and Campaigns) scope, not an automatic Lite restriction. Do not silently change its printing/revision or import Third Edition HT-as-HP and passive-defense rules. Respect the chosen source's actual options; adopting Basic Set does not enable every optional or cinematic rule. Additional magic, powers, cinematic rules and equipment require an allowed source. If a rule essential to resolution is unavailable, identify and resolve the missing parameter from that source rather than inventing an official table or cost or silently downgrading to Lite.\n\n**Sheet.** Keep the player's existing `[ENTITIES #id]`: ST, DX, IQ, HT; HP, Will, Perception, FP; Basic Speed, Basic Move, Basic Lift, encumbrance and current Move; Dodge and each usable Parry/Block; skills with base levels, points, defaults and specializations; advantages, disadvantages, self-control numbers, quirks, languages and relevant social traits; current/maximum HP and FP, wounds, posture and conditions; weapons, damage type/formula, reach/range, ammunition, readiness, armor DR by coverage, money and carried weight. Retain sources, limitations and earned changes. HP and FP are separate from HT: ordinary Fourth Edition baselines derive HP from ST and FP from HT, with purchased exceptions. Do not create classes or D&D ability modifiers.\n\n**Success rolls.** For consequential uncertainty, establish the actual trait, effective level after applicable modifiers, attempted result and time before rolling. Use real dice-tool receipts, usually `3d6`, and compare the total with the effective level. At or below succeeds, subject to critical and automatic-failure rules. Record margin, not merely pass/fail. Ordinary critical success is 3–4, also 5 at effective skill 15+, and 6 at 16+. A 17 always fails and is critical at effective skill 15 or below; 18 is critical failure. A result at least 10 above effective skill is also critical failure. Ordinary voluntary success rolls below effective skill 3 cannot succeed; active defenses and compelled resistance rolls follow their source's exceptions. Do not turn reaction rolls or damage into roll-under checks.\n\nQuick Contests compare margins: the greater margin of success or lesser margin of failure wins; ties do not create a winner by comparing raw dice. Critical labels alone do not override that margin comparison. Resistance contests may additionally require the initiator to succeed. Regular Contests repeat only as their procedure requires, with the actual elapsed duration per exchange. A normal attack and active defense are separate success rolls, not a Quick Contest. Repeated practical attempts use the source's limits, penalties, risks and elapsed effort. An authorized Luck advantage reroll or other option requires its real trigger, cooldown/use record and player decision; never reroll because a revision would read better, or charge a resource twice while reusing a receipt.\n\n**Luck and time of play.** The ordinary Luck advantage permits its specified best-of-three resolution once per hour of play; Extraordinary Luck uses 30 minutes of play, Ridiculous Luck 10. This is real play time, not elapsed fictional time: an hour's journey, a rest, a tool call or review cannot recharge it. Record the acquired variant, declared use, relevant original/replacement receipts and next eligibility against an agreed play-time/session marker, separate from the single world clock. Do not infer active play time from API latency, request timestamps, a browser reload or an unattended pause. In asynchronous play, if no reliable play-time measure exists, resolve and record a player-agreed equivalent cadence before another dependent use; label that substitute as a campaign convention. Apply other Luck variants and reroll authority only from their adopted source.\n\n**One-second combat.** Turn order normally uses Basic Speed and the source's tie rules; retain it throughout the fight. Each actor's turn overlaps other actors' turns. One cycle of everyone's opportunities advances approximately one second, not one second per actor or tool call. Choose the legal maneuver, movement, posture, ready equipment and target; respect Aim, Evaluate, Ready, Concentrate, Wait, All-Out Attack/Defense and any adopted tactical options. All-Out Attack removes active defenses until its rule boundary. Wait is not a free interrupt plus unrestricted new maneuver. Resolve awareness, surprise, visibility, reach, range, rate of fire, cover and ammunition as actually established.\n\nAfter a successful ordinary attack, permit a legal Dodge, Parry or Block if the target is aware and can react. Critical hits normally deny active defense. Shield Defense Bonus modifies eligible active defenses; DR stops penetrating damage rather than replacing defense rolls. Respect weapon readiness, defense arcs, retreat and repeated-defense limits under the selected source: Lite and full Basic Set do not provide identical repeated-Parry options. A gunshot is not generally blockable/parryable by ordinary equipment; Dodge represents avoiding the line of fire, not seeing and outrunning a bullet.\n\n**Damage, injury and recovery.** Roll actual damage, apply relevant DR and any armor divisor, then damage-type wounding modifiers to penetrating damage. Track HP injury separately from basic damage and FP loss. Use established injury tolerances and location rules, not a universal critical-damage multiplier. Shock normally penalizes next-turn DX/IQ-based actions by injury, capped at −4, without penalizing active defenses. Apply major-wound HT checks, knockdown, stunning and recovery, low-HP/FP movement/defense effects, consciousness, mortal wounds and successive death thresholds as the selected rules require. An ordinary body's automatic-death threshold is −5 times maximum HP; do not import D&D death saves or resurrection. Healing, first aid, sleep and FP recovery have their actual limits and time; neither a new scene nor point spending automatically heals injury.\n\n**Social and special abilities.** Preserve relevant Status, Reputation, Rank, Duty, Patron/Ally/Enemy, loyalties, debts, family ties and practical bribery terms where established and consequential; do not give every NPC a purchasable weakness. Reaction rolls are normally `3d6` plus reaction modifiers with higher outcomes better, used when a reaction is undetermined. Influence uses its actual skill/Will contest and source-specific results, including Diplomacy's exception; it is not unlimited mind control or guaranteed information. Self-control disadvantages, Fright Checks and defined mind-affecting abilities apply their real consequences and duration. A generic refusal boundary grants no invented immunity, but neither does a good reaction grant unknown facts or consent outside the effect's scope. Only adopted systems grant magic/powers; track actual prerequisites, skill, concentration, resistance, FP/other costs, maintenance and expiration.\n\n**Point advancement.** Use a campaign-owned `[MISC #character_progression]` point ledger with `system: \"gurps4e\"`, not D&D XP/level validation. Preserve the baseline sheet value, earned bonus points and unspent balance. Record dated unique awards and each authorized purchase with before/after values, point-cost difference, source, prerequisites and pending player choice. Apply only legal permitted improvements; buying off a disadvantage needs the governing conditions, not automatic erasure of debts, scars or history. Recompute affected derived statistics and skill defaults together with the sheet; preserve spent resources and ongoing conditions. Training consumes time only under its applicable method. Do not double-award for a repeated event or reroll acquisition on a repair.\n\nWholly off-screen processes use the recorded deterministic campaign convention, explicitly a simulation convention rather than universal GURPS rules. It does not replace direct encounter dice. Resolve each real interval once and keep wounds, temporary modifiers, maintenance and independent schedules consistent with the one clock and selected quality budget.\n",
  "cyberpunk_red": "[GAME SYSTEM PROFILE — CYBERPUNK RED]\nUse Cyberpunk RED core rules with recorded errata, allowed supplements and campaign exceptions. RED, Cyberpunk 2020, the Jumpstart Kit and Edgerunners Mission Kit are not interchangeable rulesets; require an explicit source for additions. This profile does not impose Night City, a date, a mercenary occupation, a dystopian tone or an attitude on the player's character. Keep the quality profile's N−1 preparation, finite inventories, independent NPCs, knowledge separation and one clock.\n\n**Character state.** Preserve the supplied handle, Roles and Role Ability ranks, INT/REF/DEX/TECH/COOL/WILL/LUCK/MOVE/BODY/EMP, skill levels and their STAT-based totals, current/max HP, Serious Wound threshold, wound state, Death Save penalty, Critical Injuries, current/max Humanity and derived EMP. Track remaining LUCK, Reputation and its established causes, cyberware and slot requirements, weapons with damage/ammunition/ROF/quality, separate head/body armor SP and penalties, eurobucks, gear and relevant housing/lifestyle obligations. Preserve established Lifepath facts, contacts and responsibilities; do not generate the player's past, identity, enemies or intimate ties without authorization. Keep additional NET, vehicle and fabrication details only when relevant to prepared interactions.\n\n**Skill resolution.** For an uncertain direct action, fix the task duration, appropriate STAT and skill, circumstances, DV or opposition before calling the dice tool. Roll `1d10` + STAT + skill + applicable modifiers. The acting character must beat the DV; a tie favors the defender. On the initial natural 10 roll exactly one additional `1d10` and add it; on an initial natural 1 roll exactly one additional `1d10` and subtract it from the original total. That second die never explodes or implodes again. These critical labels modify the total; they do not automatically determine success, inflict damage or invent mishaps. Retain individual die results, not merely a narrated total. Spend LUCK before a check when the player chooses, apply its actual scope, and track refresh at an established session boundary rather than every message. A failed attempt normally needs improved chances before retrying; changed tools, complementary checks and extra time must be real and cost their actual time/resources.\n\n**Combat and shared time.** One round is approximately three seconds for all participants. Track REF-based initiative, each actor's Move Action and one other Action, legal split movement, ROF, held actions and reloads. An ROF 2 attack permits its actual two attacks within one Attack Action; it is not two unrestricted actions. Ranged attacks use REF + the weapon's skill against its weapon/range DV, or eligible evasion under the applicable core rules. Melee attacks use DEX + the appropriate skill against DEX + Evasion. Respect range, cover, visibility, ammunition, weapon quality, autofire requirements and special maneuvers. Do not substitute D&D AC, bonus actions, six-second rounds or advantage. Record relevant range brackets/DVs from the actual weapon source; do not generate a convenient hit threshold after the roll.\n\n**Damage and survival.** Roll actual weapon damage dice through the tool. Apply the struck location's SP, armor penetration and ablation under the attack's rules; armor reduces damage rather than the chance to hit. Keep head/body SP separate, apply relevant armor penalties and do not stack armor layers as extra SP. Called shots use their actual penalty, ROF and location effect. Two or more sixes on qualifying damage cause a Critical Injury and its bonus damage, not an ordinary d10 check's natural 10; use the actual location's injury table and genuine required dice. Track injury-specific penalties and treatment separately from HP. At Serious Wound and Mortally Wounded thresholds apply the correct penalties. While Mortally Wounded, roll a Death Save at turn start: `1d10` plus accumulated Death Save penalty must be below BODY; natural 10 always fails. One failure kills; increase the penalty for subsequent saves until stabilization resets it to its injury-based baseline. Death Saves do not use ordinary check explosion/implosion or LUCK. Stabilization, treatment, surgery, repair and healing consume their actual time, skills, materials and money; a scene transition does not heal or restore armor.\n\n**Cyberware, networks and resources.** Apply installed cyberware's actual mechanical benefits, Humanity Loss, maximum-Humanity effects, prerequisites and capacity limits. Humanity, EMP and current mood are different records; neither the Social focus nor a dramatic conversation grants free mechanical recovery. Use the source's therapy and installation/removal rules. Prepare relevant NET Architecture, access points, defenses and files before interaction, preserving closed information and hardware access limits. Before a NET action is resolved, record the adopted source's NET/Meat action-budget relationship, Interface-rank budget and allowed movement, then enforce that relationship within the same combat interval. Merely tracking two kinds of action does not grant both budgets: never add NET Actions on top of an already spent ordinary Action unless the adopted rule expressly permits that combination. If the governing relationship is unavailable, identify it as unresolved before spending a dependent action; do not promote Jumpstart or Edgerunners Mission Kit wording to full-core RAW. NET checks are not interchangeable with ordinary STAT + skill checks. Do not let an ordinary Agent or any convenient screen become a hackable Architecture without its established mechanics.\n\n**Advancement and social rules.** Maintain one dated `[MISC #character_progression]` record with `system: \"cyberpunk_red\"`, baseline ranks, unique completed-session/challenge IP awards under the established policy, total earned, spent, unspent, purchases with governing costs, and pending player choices. Use a campaign-owned RED schema, not D&D's version-1 ledger schema or a second parallel progression block. IP buys legal Skill/Role Ability improvement; it is not D&D cumulative level XP and does not automatically raise every STAT, HP or equipment quality. Confirm prerequisites, cost multipliers and allowed rank changes from the actual source before spending, then update sheet and balance together. The extension's D&D progression validator does not validate this record. Ordinary conversation, persuasion, bribery, interrogation and trade use their own skills and actual stakes. Establish relevant loyalties, debts, incentives, family ties and limits before adjudication, without mandatory vulnerabilities or invented relationship scores. Use Role Abilities' actual benefits and limits; social success never creates unknown information or rewrites the player's chosen feelings. Any permitted coercive effect applies only within its source-defined scope.\n\n**Off-screen convention and uncertainty.** Preserve a recorded deterministic off-screen protocol. If absent, explicitly record this campaign house convention: fixed d10 contribution 5, no critical explosion/implosion, ordinary average damage without randomly generated Critical Injuries, ties favor defenders, stable initiative by REF then actor ID. This is not official RED and never replaces direct-interaction dice or guarantees success. Retain actual rolls and spent resources through review, repair and network retries; bookkeeping never licenses a fresh result. Where a source-specific weapon, Role, injury, IP cost or optional subsystem is unknown, identify the missing parameter and resolve it from the governing source before applying a consequential result.\n",
  "vtm5e": "[GAME SYSTEM PROFILE — VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE FIFTH EDITION (V5), v1]\nUse V5 tabletop mechanics, the chronicle's recorded printing/errata, character sources and explicitly adopted supplements. Do not mix V20, Requiem, Mind's Eye Theatre, other World of Darkness games or a different edition. This profile does not supply metaplot, clans present in the city, factions, obligatory horror, a romance or an adversary. A selected hopeful tone does not remove Hunger mechanics; selecting V5 does not rewrite the existing setting or turn a supplied mortal into a vampire.\n\n**Sheet and sources.** In the actor's ENTITIES block retain relevant Attributes, Skills/specialties, Advantages/Flaws, clan and bane if applicable, generation, Blood Potency, Hunger, Humanity, Chronicle Tenets, Convictions/Touchstones, Ambition/Desire, known Discipline powers and their acquisition sources. Track Health and Willpower maxima and separately marked superficial/aggravated damage, armor, equipment, conditions, Compulsions, blood bonds, temporary effects and resource use. Keep source-dependent Blood Surge, mending and feeding parameters rather than assume every vampire has the same values. Do not create missing player convictions, relationships or powers without a creation choice. Preserve established actors' relevant incentives and loyalties before social resolution; no compulsory vice, bribe price or exploitable relative.\n\n**Tests and receipts.** Form the source-defined d10 pool, commonly Attribute + Skill, with specialties, penalties and situational modifiers. Fix Difficulty or the opposition before rolling; 6–10 each count as a success. Every pair of 10s contributes four successes instead of two; an unpaired 10 contributes one. Meeting a simple Difficulty succeeds; apply source-defined contests, margins, ties and critical-win rules. Never treat the pool sum as the number of successes. Use returned individual faces and retain their identities.\n\nFor affected vampiric pools, replace regular dice with Hunger dice up to the smaller of Hunger and pool size: Hunger adds no extra dice. Record separate labeled regular and Hunger receipts, including empty subpools. They have the same numerical faces but different consequences. Do not substitute Hunger into Rouse checks, Willpower or Humanity rolls or other excluded pools. A successful critical involving a Hunger 10 is a messy critical; a failed affected test with a Hunger 1 is a bestial failure. A Hunger 10 alone does not make a critical, and a Hunger 1 does not by itself make a successful test fail. Resolve the applicable Beast consequence under the actual rules and circumstances, without invented information, arbitrary loot or a preselected dramatic punishment.\n\n**Willpower and Blood.** A permitted Willpower reroll costs one superficial Willpower damage and replaces up to three chosen non-Hunger dice. Respect the once-per-test limit and excluded tests; Hunger dice cannot be rerolled this way. Retain original faces, selected indices, replacement receipts and recomputed outcome; do not take the best face independently unless a source permits that. Optional spending remains the player's choice unless delegated. A technical retry or review does not authorize another attempt.\n\nApply the adopted source's distinct **superficial and aggravated Willpower recovery** triggers, amounts and limits; record eligibility and actual recovery once. Preserve the agreed game-session marker when a recovery rule depends on it, separately from fictional nights and scenes. A model message, review, API wait or reload is not a new game session. Do not generalize a Quick-Start scenario's no-recovery restriction to a full V5 chronicle, or restore all Willpower merely because a scene ended or the character woke. Resolve an unavailable recovery parameter from the governing source before applying it; do not import another World of Darkness game's recovery rules or invent a numerical rate.\n\nA Rouse check is a separate d10: 6+ avoids the Hunger increase; failure ordinarily adds one Hunger rather than making the paid effect fail. Apply actual timing, Blood Potency reroll eligibility, feeding restrictions and Hunger-5 limits. Never subtract a generic blood-point pool or refill Hunger because a scene ended. Feeding requires established access, actual time and source-defined consequences. Track waking checks, mending and ongoing powers on the single clock; do not resolve an extra night whenever a model stage runs.\n\n**Conflict and harm.** Declare intent and opposing responses; resolve physical and social conflict with the actual pools, margins, weapon effects and Health/Willpower target. V5 turns have duration appropriate to the action, not a universal six seconds. Apply superficial/aggravated classification and any halving, armor conversion, impairment, overflow, mending, torpor or destruction to the correct creature and tracker. Fire, sunlight, a stake and ordinary bullets have different rules; never infer vampire armor or healing from D&D. Record exposure, source, paid healing and elapsed intervals. A social defeat has its rules-defined stakes, not unrestricted ownership of another character's beliefs.\n\n**Humanity and powers.** Track Stains with their actual causes and apply Chronicle Tenets, Convictions, Touchstones and Remorse at their proper boundaries. Humanity is not sanity, an affection score or permission to impose an unrelated moral code. Use source-defined frenzy/Compulsion triggers and resistance, not automatic loss of control on every Hunger increase. Dominate, Presence, blood bonds and other effects retain their specific prerequisites, exceptions, resistance, scope and ending conditions. Do not invent immunity from a generic refusal boundary, nor turn emotional influence into unlimited commands, unknown knowledge or permanent devotion. A memory-changing power can alter an actor's memory without retroactively changing objective history.\n\n**Advancement.** Use the campaign-owned `[MISC #character_progression]` record with `system: \"vtm5e\"`. Record dated, uniquely identified XP awards, total earned/spent/unspent XP, purchases and pending selections. Use the adopted V5 costs, prerequisites, training/source requirements and actual choices for Attributes, Skills, specialties, Disciplines, Blood Potency and other permitted improvements. Record each cost before spending; do not invent a missing cost table or import D&D levels, proficiency or automatic HP gains. Existing powers, injuries, Stains, Hunger and resource deficits survive advancement and compression. Use the common profile contract for wholly off-screen deterministic house adjudication; it is distinct from official V5 dice rules.\n",
  "swade": "[GAME SYSTEM PROFILE — SAVAGE WORLDS ADVENTURE EDITION (SWADE), v1]\nUse Adventure Edition, the recorded printing/errata, setting rules, Edges, Hindrances and explicitly adopted companions. Do not substitute Deluxe/Explorer's Edition, Pathfinder for Savage Worlds or a setting's special rules without adoption. This profile supplies mechanics, not Deadlands, a required pulp tone, a protagonist's destiny or a larger preparation horizon. Powers, ancestries and gear must belong to the established campaign.\n\n**Sheet.** Retain Agility, Smarts, Spirit, Strength and Vigor as die types; Skills and linked Attributes; Wild Card/Extra status; Edges/Hindrances with requirements and sources; Pace/running die, Parry, Toughness with Armor separately, Size, Wounds, Fatigue, Shaken and other conditions. Track gear, ammunition/reloads, ranges, AP, damage dice, powers, Arcane Background/skill, Power Points, active effects, Bennies by owner and the distinct GM pool. An important NPC is not automatically granted Wild Card resilience after a bad result. No D&D AC, Hit Dice, proficiency or generic spell-slot system.\n\n**Trait resolution.** The ordinary TN is 4; use applicable Parry, opposed resolution and situational modifiers instead where required. Each full four above the governing TN/opposition is a raise. An unskilled attempt ordinarily uses d4−2; apply source exceptions. A Wild Card normally rolls the Trait die and a d6 Wild Die, choosing the higher completed result after applicable modifiers, not adding them. Extras normally have no Wild Die. Preserve separate labeled faces and ace chains. When a die aces, roll that same die again and add; repeat as needed. Do not explode a running die or another roll whose rules exclude acing.\n\nFor an ordinary single-Trait roll, natural 1 on both Trait and Wild Die is a Critical Failure, regardless of modifiers; no ordinary Benny reroll can erase it. Apply the actual Extra and multiple-Trait-dice critical-failure rules rather than generalize the single-die shortcut. Multiple-Trait actions get their source-defined number of Wild Dice, not one per projectile. Keep original and replacement receipts; any permitted reroll's Critical Failure must be accepted even if an earlier total was better.\n\n**Bennies and choices.** Track awards/spending once, with owner, reason, balance and agreed game-session identity. Under ordinary SWADE, a Wild Card player starts a session with three Bennies; the GM's shared pool begins with one per player character, and each GM Wild Card has two personal Bennies as well. Keep those pools and their source-defined spending permissions distinct. Apply established Edge/setting exceptions and session refresh/expiry rules; never replenish a previously spent pool simply because its actor enters view or a block is revised. A message, reload, repair or technical retry is not a new session. Legal uses include Trait/damage rerolls, Soak, removing Shaken, drawing a new Action Card and applicable Power Point recovery. Apply their actual timing, eligible pool, cost and keep semantics. Do not silently spend the player's Bennies or disable them because deterministic world preparation exists.\n\n**Initiative and time.** Combat rounds are about six seconds shared by all participants. Maintain Action Cards, current round, Hold, remaining deck and discards. Deal from a standard 54-card deck including two Jokers; resolve rank descending, suit ties Spades, Hearts, Diamonds, Clubs, plus adopted draw effects. A Joker permits flexible action timing and +2 Trait/damage rolls; apply the actual Joker Benny awards and reshuffle at the end of that round. Use source-defined redraw and Hold/interrupt rules. Repeating the same resolved turn does not deal again.\n\nThe extension does not supply a card engine. Use verifiable manual draws, an actually available card tool, or this explicit campaign implementation: persist a fixed ordered list of remaining unique card IDs; use a real supported 1dN roll for the current list length N, remove that indexed card and record the receipt/mapping. Apply real reset/shuffle boundaries; do not invent a shuffled order, reuse a removed card or claim a nonexistent card tool. If no verifiable method is available, leave the draw unresolved. Wholly off-screen deterministic resolution follows the common contract as a campaign convention, without pretend random card faces.\n\nDeclare actions before rolling; normally up to three actions with −2 to all for each beyond the first, subject to specific exceptions. Respect movement, reach, running, cover, range, Tests/Support, ammunition and reactions. Melee normally targets Parry; ranged attacks ordinarily use TN 4 plus actual modifiers. Damage sums its separate acing dice without a Wild Die. An attack raise normally adds one acing d6, not one per raise. Apply AP only to relevant Armor.\n\n**Damage and recovery.** Compare damage against effective Toughness. A simple success causes Shaken; damage causing Shaken again can inflict a Wound. Each damage raise inflicts a Wound; use the correct combined rule rather than add an extra Wound simply because an already-Shaken target suffers raises. An ordinary Extra is incapacitated by a Wound; a standard Wild Card can sustain three before a further Wound incapacitates. Apply penalties and source exceptions. Soak costs a Benny and uses Vigor immediately against that attack's pending Wounds; do not apply those pending Wound penalties before the roll. Each success/raise soaks one; soaking all removes Shaken. Recover from Shaken with the source-defined start-of-turn Spirit roll or a legal Benny. Keep Fatigue separate and preserve its actual causes, penalties and recovery conditions; no automatic full recovery at scene end.\n\n**Story influence and advancement.** The core permits GM-approved Benny influence over story details. Before any dependent action, explicitly resolve a requested exception to ordinary N−1/closed-state preparation out of character, including permitted scope and cost, then record it as an authorized campaign edit. Preserve established history and facts unless the player explicitly authorizes a retcon. An unspent Benny or casual search cannot secretly create convenient loot; do not quietly forbid legitimate negotiated story influence either.\n\nUse the campaign-owned `[MISC #character_progression]` record with `system: \"swade\"` for awarded Advances and applied/pending choices under the agreed session/objective cadence. Preserve Rank, current Advance count and prerequisite/source evidence; apply the adopted Rank thresholds, skill/Attribute limits, Edge prerequisites and Legendary exceptions. Do not invent XP awards or import D&D levels. Advancement neither resets Bennies nor heals Wounds/Fatigue. Powers and social mechanics follow their actual source and the common actor-preparation rules, with no universal bribery vulnerability or unsupported immunity.\n"
};
